WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.880
The Large Magellanic Cloud.

00:02.522 --> 00:06.590
This photograph of the Large Magellanic Cloud lines up with our sky.

00:07.245 --> 00:18.856
The biggest of our galaxy's companions and the fourth-largest galaxy in the group, it is a hundred and sixty thousand light-years away: pairs of its stars that eclipse each other tell us how far.
